{"author":{"id":"609bf866d4a5d716c19faf5d617b3bf3de478230d29602d72aad5aa90a80466f"},"ops":[{"type":1,"timestamp":1790958912,"nonce":"Okr4psZT2cTmRWZXK/xBeASK91Y=","title":"Interpreter: an exception from a method called through a generic interface cannot be caught","message":"In interp and hybrid modes, an exception thrown by a method reached through a\ngeneric interface escapes the caller's `try` and aborts the program. `--mode\njit` catches it. Same on the installed build of 2026-09-28 and on\ntarget/release of 2026-09-30 (HEAD b3e87e4), macOS arm64.\n\n    interface IG\u003cT\u003e { function f():T; }\n\n    class CG implements IG\u003cInt\u003e {\n        public function new() {}\n        public function f():Int { throw \"boom\"; }\n    }\n\n    class Repro {\n        static function main() {\n            var g:IG\u003cInt\u003e = new CG();\n            try g.f() catch (e:Dynamic) trace(\"caught: \" + e);  // aborts in interp/hybrid\n            trace(\"returned\");\n        }\n    }\n\n    haxe -main Repro -hl repro.hl \u0026\u0026 ash --mode interp repro.hl\n\nOutput:\n\n    [ash] uncaught exception: String \"boom\"\n    hlp_throw called without active trap; aborting\n      ...\n      #7 hl_throw\n      #8 HLInterpreter::raise_stub_bridge_failure\n      #9 HLInterpreter::execute_entrypoint::fiber_closure_runner\n      #10 hlp_vcall_dyn\n      #11 HLInterpreter::op_call_method\n      #12 HLInterpreter::ssa_step\n\nThe same throw through a non-generic interface (`interface I { function\nf():Int; }`), or through a direct call on the class, is caught in every mode.\nSo the generic slot sends the call through `hlp_vcall_dyn` and the closure\nrunner. The callee's exception comes back to the bridge as an error, and the\nbridge rethrows it with `hl_throw` into the C trap chain, where the\ninterpreted caller's `try` is not registered.\n\nFound through ashui, where `Computed\u003cT\u003e` is an abstract over `IComputed\u003cT\u003e`.\nA computed whose closure throws rethrows from `get()`, and under interp or\nhybrid that aborts the program instead of reaching the caller's `try`.","files":null}]}